{
  "note": "The Khumbu Icefall, Base Camp to Camp 1, in the parts the sources name (route.icefall-parts, #172): Base Camp's tents on the moraine of the Khumbu Glacier (route.base-camp-ground), Crampon Point where it ends and the first rope is fixed; the Popcorn's jumbled blocks, short walls with a ladder each and the first crevasses, with snow bridges between them; the maze of towers, tall walls and wide crevasses, where the ladders are lashed end to end (route.icefall-ladders-lashed) and the first seracs stand over the route; the Football Field, a flat at route.football-field-altitude under the seracs; the Upper Icefall's tallest walls and longest ladders under the West Shoulder's hanging glacier; and the open snow of the Western Cwm, its last crevasses and its slope under Nuptse's wall, to Camp 1. Drawn at 1/route.drawn-scale of its length and its rise (docs/conventions/slope-physics.md → The slope), with every wall, crevasse and ladder at life size: 280 m of ground rising 45 m stand for the Icefall's length and the camps' altitudes, which the knowledge base gives (route.icefall-length, route.base-camp-altitude, route.camp-1-altitude), so the walls' metres up are paid back by walls down behind the blocks and towers, each with its ladder, as the sources' ladders go down as well as up. Every sloping segment is a Pythagorean triple, so the corners, where the ladders' ends and the ropes' anchors go, are at whole metres along the ground. The walls grow from the Popcorn's 3–4 m to the maze's 6–8 m, two or three ladders lashed, and the Upper Icefall's 9 and 11 m; the crevasses, 3–8 m across, are 15–36 m deep. Each wall's and each crevasse's ladder has a rope of its own from end to end, and from the maze up the ropes run in a line and share their anchors, as the fixed line does; below it they leave the easy ground between the Popcorn's ladders free. The snow on the ground (layout.snow) is the game's, not the sources': it rises and falls by a few tens of centimetres over a few metres and rounds the breaks of slope, and the climbers walk on it, slower over its hummocks (#168); it lies level by the walls, at the ladders' ends, and over the camps and trodden flat for layout.snow.trodden metres round them, where the climbs set off and arrive, so they stand where the line has them. The camps are the flat at each end: the tents stand on them, and reaching Camp 1's is the arrival. The expedition sets off on the sources' hour (time.base-camp-departure) and the bodies are made up, as the stand-in's were, until the camp screen (#53) and the acclimatization (#51) set them.",
